/-
Johnson/FrontRoad/ThinProverSpec.lean: definitions and statements only. A CONTROL: NOT THE HONEST
PROVER. The thin prover has, of all the description's members, a half at the twenty-five places of
the smallness test alone, each with the one pinned part, which sends nothing; at every other member
it has no half: it has no part that sends anything. No run of it that a verifier accepts is claimed,
and nothing on completeness follows. What it is for: at a written book, written rows and this
prover, ALL premises of the implication Spec.sessionStops_of_cellsOwn
(Johnson/FrontRoad/CellsOwnAtSpec.lean), at mats := matsOf Zp.p.X, hold together, under the four
public premises and ReadsAs Zp.p.X cells' e, which two pairs of letters meet (Spec.readsAs_id,
Spec.readsAs_cells, Johnson/FrontRoad/TraceOwnAtSpec.lean): so that implication does not hold idly
for want of a book, rows and a prover. Nor is its end empty for want of a tied request: at Yes :=
RyesZ Z some tied request has a trace at these rows (Spec.ownAt_speaks, that file, which stands at
every book and all rows). Proved in Johnson/FrontRoad/ThinProver.lean.
Terms of this folder: Johnson/FrontRoad/Spec.lean.

What this file has (namespace OnBytes.FrontRoad).
  thinFirst Zp cells   at most twenty-five halves, and twenty-five under scope, the reading and
      LaidAt (Spec.matsOf_fits, Johnson/FrontRoad/CellsAreTraceSpec.lean): at each written place
      k8PlaceAt l, l below 25, at which parOwn Zp (matsOf Zp.p.X) names parameters P, the one part
      quietStop (smallStop cells P) (windowShare P.1).
  thinBook F ks   a book: for each member of each chain one row, at the member's place and the part
      0, with as many coins of the base field as the member declares mask words; no entry; for each
      place of ks the cut [1].
  thinHalves Zp cells' H₀, thinAt Zp e H₀   H₀ with its first halves laid as thinFirst Zp cells' and
      no half in the shared and the second chain; H₀ with its range test laid as «true» and its
      trace field as modelAt Zp.p.X e (Johnson/FrontRoad/TraceOwnAtSpec.lean).
  thinB Zp Np cF, thinG Zp Np cF cells' H₀   the book thinBook at the description and the
      twenty-five places; the rows bareSides (Johnson/FrontRoad/CarryThroughSpec.lean) of thinHalves
      at that book.
  thinP Z Zp Np cF cells' e H₀   short for provG at that book, these rows and thinAt Zp e H₀.
  Spec.thin_halves, Spec.thin_no_frame   at all public files in scope that can be read, under
      LaidAt: thinFirst meets PinHalvesAt at the description's own parameters and matsOf, at the
      first chain without its last member. Every half of thinFirst stands at a place of the kind K8,
      so none at one of the kind frame.
  Spec.thin_meets_four   a control for Johnson/FrontRoad/CarryThroughSpec.lean: at all public files
      in scope that can be read, under LaidAt and ReadsAs, a prover at the index type Cm.Idx with
      these halves and the trace function that answers e of the model's trace meets the four
      conditions of Spec.sessionStops_of_elder together.
  Spec.thinBook_word   at all public files in scope that can be read, under LaidAt: the book's own
      tests pass at thinB: ProverCoinCounts.word answers none.
  Spec.thin_ready   under the four public premises: ready returns at provG of thinG and thinAt, at
      some matrix, randomness, instance and coins.
  Spec.premises_met_together   under the four public premises and ReadsAs: at the book thinB, the
      rows thinG and the prover thinAt, the five premises on rows and prover of
      Spec.sessionStops_of_cellsOwn hold together: hR at some input, hn, h₁, h₃, and CellsOwnAt
      cells' at every Yes.
  Spec.sessionStops_at_thin   so the end of that implication holds there, under the four public
      premises and ReadsAs alone.

How it fits. Of the implication Spec.sessionStops_of_cellsOwn, which is named for the field
sessionStops (PremWDebts, E2E/BridgeDebts.lean), its file's head says that no book, rows and prover
are known at which its premises hold together. Here are such, for that one implication, at mats :=
matsOf Zp.p.X and one book, which is written for this prover. What may be said in that sentence's
place, the two never apart: «All premises of this implication hold together at one written control
(Spec.premises_met_together): a thin prover that has the twenty-five pinned parts alone and sends
nothing.» «No prover that sends a message is known at which they hold together.» Of the other
implications on that field nothing is stated here. By the text of hidB
(Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Record.lean) the sessions' private abort set reads of a prover its
trace function and, of its first and second halves, the places, each part's number of moves, and the
private and public abort tests. Words (member, half, part, public and private abort test, stated
share): Johnson/FrontRoad/SessionStopsPinned.lean. Not one of the release's goal statements.

Limits.
  NOT THE HONEST PROVER. It has no part that sends anything: at 333 of the first chain's 358
      members, and at every member of the shared and the second chain, it has no half. Nothing is
      said of a run of it beyond ready's return: no completeness is claimed, and no run that a
      verifier accepts; that no verifier accepts one is not claimed either.
  The rows are bareSides: their simulators read nothing and their four letters are laid as «true».
      No other field of PremWDebts is meant to be had at them; so nothing is said on the whole of
      PremWDebts.
  The book is written for this prover. It is no book that is computed from the public files
      independently of the prover's sides, which is what that type's docstring asks of a book that
      is to be a check.
  The trace field is laid so by definition (modelAt): the model's trace, through e. No program runs
      it.
  H₀ is a letter: of it there are left the named element, the two own states at the start, and meet;
      provG overwrites stored and key. In thinG it bears types alone: the rows are made of
      thinFirst. Spec.thin_meets_four meets four of the premises of Spec.sessionStops_of_elder; hR
      at the image and the two equations on the rows are not among them, and H₀'s range test is a
      letter there. The library's own test halvedAll says false at the thin prover (said here
      without a theorem).
  That the library's honest rows have the same private abort set as the thin prover is not said: it
      would want, at the least, that their other halves' private abort tests never fire, that no
      public abort test of theirs fires earlier, and that the reader yields the same cells of
      trace: each another house's matter.
  That the private abort set has a member at any tied request is said nowhere: the bound may bound
      the empty set. Whether a pinned test fires at some challenge is a fact on the numbers of the
      model's trace, of which nothing is known here. No value is given for the bound. The full size
      alone. At public files that do not meet the public premises the statements hold idly; these
      are met together at two stored sets, in the side library: at VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles in one statement
      (premises_met_at_full, AtFullSide/Top/LaidAtFull.lean); at VerifierAndGoals.zGap in two
      (headMember_zGap, AtFullSide/Top/HeadMemberAtGap.lean: the fields scope, reads and laid of its
      head; theLive_zGap, AtFullSide/Top/LiveAtPolicies.lean).
  Nothing is said on hiding, completeness or soundness.
-/
